From 3380a8ece93fc64d14ab44cba629cbffc0032a18 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hans Hubner <hans@huebner.org>
Date: Sat, 27 Jun 2026 14:32:05 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] imapclient: add X-GM-LABELS (X-GM-EXT-1) FETCH support

Gmail's IMAP server advertises X-GM-EXT-1 and exposes each message's set of
labels via the X-GM-LABELS FETCH data item. The client previously hard-errored
on this msg-att ("unsupported msg-att name") in handleFetch, breaking any
FETCH that requested it.

Add first-class support:

  - imap.FetchOptions.GmailLabels requests the item; writeFetchItems emits the
    X-GM-LABELS atom.
  - handleFetch parses the parenthesised label list (backslash-prefixed system
    labels such as \\Inbox / \\Sent, and astring user labels which may be
    quoted and modified-UTF-7 encoded) into FetchItemDataGmailLabels.
  - FetchMessageBuffer.GmailLabels is populated by Collect via populateItemData.

A scripted-server unit test covers the round-trip (mixed system and quoted
user labels, including a label with a space and one with a slash).
---
 fetch.go                       |   1 +
 imapclient/fetch.go            |  66 ++++++++++++++++++-
 imapclient/fetch_gmail_test.go | 117 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 183 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 imapclient/fetch_gmail_test.go

diff --git a/fetch.go b/fetch.go
